  "worked_solution": "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of the line $8x-y=2,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x-y & =2 \\\\ -y & =-8x+2 \\\\ y & =8x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $8.$\n\nFrom the given options, the only line that has a slope of $8$ is $y=8x-3.$",
